  <content>
  <section><title>Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive Property</title>
<para>The Distributive Property can be used to remove parentheses as you simplify expressions.</para>

<note>
  <para> <emphasis> DISTRIBUTIVE PROPERTY </emphasis> </para>
  <hr/>
  <para>
    <m:math display="block">
      <m:semantics>
        <m:mrow>
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mtable>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mtext>If</m:mtext>
                  <m:mspace width="0.2em"/>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mspace width="0.2em"/>
                  <m:mtext>are real numbers, then</m:mtext>
                </m:mtd>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
              <m:mtr/>
              <m:mtr/>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd columnalign="right">
                  <m:mtext>Also,</m:mtext>
                </m:mtd>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
            </m:mtable>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:mrow>
        <m:annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mtable>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mtext>If</m:mtext>
                  <m:mspace width="0.2em"/>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mspace width="0.2em"/>
                  <m:mtext>are real numbers, then</m:mtext>
                </m:mtd>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
              <m:mtr/>
              <m:mtr/>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd columnalign="right">
                  <m:mtext>Also,</m:mtext>
                </m:mtd>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
              <m:mtr>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd/>
                <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mtd>
              </m:mtr>
            </m:mtable>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:annotation-xml>
      </m:semantics>
    </m:math>
  </para>
</note>

<para>Simplify:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(3(x+4)\)It may help to use arrows to show the Distributive Property.
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1baa8e4eada73ed91541fd584befe88f8f331baf"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(-11(4-3a)\)
    Use arrows to show the Distributive Property. 
    <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/300ffabeac240ceeca330110ced133a3c5a87ffd"/></media></figure></item>
</list>
<title> Try It: Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive Property </title>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Simplify: \(-2(4y+1)\).</para>
  
  <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Here is how to simplify expressions using the Distributive Property.</para>
  
  <para>Use arrows to show the Distributive Property.</para>
  
  <para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5a1f98b219936a55d46552d0be26009bdaccb8eb"/></media></figure></para>
  
  <para>Use the Distributive Property.
    \(-2 \cdot 4y+(-2) \cdot 1\)</para>
  
  <para>Multiply.
    \(-8y+(-2)\)</para>
  
  <para>Simplify.
    \(-8y-2\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Check Your Understanding</title><exercise data-content-id="fe2725a9-e34e-4c6a-ba93-4368602af0de" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Which expression is equivalent to \(4(5-2a)\)?</para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(20-2a\)</para><para>\(20+2a\)</para><para>\(20-8a\)</para><para>\(20+8a\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! Check yourself: Multiply the factor outside the parentheses by each term inside the parentheses. </para><para>Try again. Let’s try again a different way: To use the Distributive Property, multiply the factor outside the parentheses by each term inside the parentheses.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<title>Videos </title>
<para>Watch the first 2 minutes and 40 seconds of the video to see how to use the Distributive Property to simplify expressions. </para>
